ibrary that provides essential mathematical operations for 3D transformations in WebGL:\n- It handles perspective, rotation, translation and other matrix operations\n- It\u0027s working correctly and doesn\u0027t affect how many circular cross-sections are drawn\n- The issue was in our vertex generation and rendering approach, not in the matrix transformations\n\n### 3. What Changed Under the Hood\n- **Segment optimization**: Increased uSegments to 120 and vSegments to 40 for smoother curves\n- **Explicit circular cross-sections**: Now generating exactly 60 complete circles along the length\n- **Improved rendering**: Each circle is now rendered as a closed loop\n- **Better distribution**: The circles are evenly distributed throughout the entire shape\n\n### How to Verify\nWhen you refresh the page, you\u0027ll now see:\n1. An alert confirming \&quot;EXACTLY 60 circles\&quot; \n2. Debug panel showing \&quot;EXACTLY 60 circles\&quot;\n3. Console log showing \&quot;Generated 60 circular cross-sections\&quot;\n4. A visually much more detailed model with 60 distinct circular cross-sections\n\nThis approach gives you direct control over the number of circles. If you want even more, you can easily change the `numCircles` value in the `generateVLines` function to any number you want.&quot;}]},{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Good all it working but can you replace everything on the index html\nand remove all additional logic \n\nI want it to draw in index.html my cupoid but in color green&quot;}],&quot;context&quot;:[{&quot;file_path&quot;:&quot;test.html&quot;,&quot;code_text&quot;:&quot;\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\r\n\u003chtml lang\u003d\&quot;en\&quot;\u003e\r\n\u003chead\u003e\r\n    \u003cmeta charset\u003d\&quot;UTF-8\&quot;\u003e\r\n    \u003cmeta name\u003d\&quot;viewport\&quot; content\u003d\&quot;width\u003ddevice-width, initial-scale\u003d1.0\&quot;\u003e\r\n    \u003ctitle\u003eServe