radius that creates the distinctive horn-like shape.\u003c/p\u003e\n 86|            \n 87|            \u003ch2\u003eMathematical Definition\u003c/h2\u003e\n 88|            \u003cp\u003eThe Cornucopia surface is defined by the following parametric equations:\u003c/p\u003e\n 89|            \n 90|            \u003cdiv class\u003d\&quot;math-formula\&quot;\u003e\n 91|                \u003cstrong\u003eRadius:\u003c/strong\u003e R(u) \u003d e\u003csup\u003epu\u003c/sup\u003e where p \u003d 0.1\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n 92|                \n 93|                \u003cstrong\u003eParametric Equations:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n 94|                x(u,v) \u003d R(u) · cos(u) · (1 + m · cos(v))\u003cbr\u003e\n 95|                y(u,v) \u003d R(u) · sin(u) · (1 + m · cos(v))\u003cbr\u003e\n 96|                z(u,v) \u003d R(u) · m · sin(v)\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n 97|                \n 98|                \u003cstrong\u003eWhere:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n 99|                - p \u003d 0.1 (expansion rate parameter)\u003cbr\u003e\n100|                - m \u003d 0.2 (cross-section size parameter)\u003cbr\u003e\n101|                - 0 ≤ u ≤ 4π (lengthwise parameter)\u003cbr\u003e\n102|                - 0 ≤ v ≤ 2π (cross-section parameter)\n103|            \u003c/div\u003e\n104|            \n105|            \u003ch2\u003eVisualization Features\u003c/h2\u003e\n106|            \u003cul\u003e\n107|                \u003cli\u003e60 circular cross-sections for detailed rendering\u003c/li\u003e\n108|                \u003cli\u003eGreen wireframe for high visibility\u003c/li\u003e\n109|                \u003cli\u003eInteractive rotation using mouse or touch\u003c/li\u003e\n110|                \u003cli\u003eElongated shape with oval cross-sections\u003c/li\u003e\n111|            \u003c/ul\u003e\n112|        \u003c/div\u003e\n113|        \n114|        \u003cdiv id\u003d\&quot;canvas-holder\&quot;\u003e\n115|            \u003ccanvas width\u003d\&quot;800\&quot; heigh