 Cornucopia is a special case of a spiral-shaped surface \&quot;Shell without vertex\&quot;. It\u0027s a cyclic surface with generatrix circles of variable radius that creates the distinctive horn-like shape.\u003c/p\u003e\n245|            \n246|            \u003ch2\u003eMathematical Definition\u003c/h2\u003e\n247|            \u003cp\u003eThe Cornucopia surface is defined by the following parametric equations:\u003c/p\u003e\n248|            \n249|            \u003cdiv class\u003d\&quot;math-formula\&quot;\u003e\n250|                \u003cstrong\u003eParametric Equations:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n251|                x(u,v) \u003d [e\u003csup\u003emu\u003c/sup\u003e + e\u003csup\u003epu\u003c/sup\u003ecos(v)]cos(u)\u003cbr\u003e\n252|                y(u,v) \u003d [e\u003csup\u003emu\u003c/sup\u003e + e\u003csup\u003epu\u003c/sup\u003ecos(v)]sin(u)\u003cbr\u003e\n253|                z(u,v) \u003d e\u003csup\u003epu\u003c/sup\u003esin(v)\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n254|                \n255|                \u003cstrong\u003eWhere:\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n256|                - p \u003d 0.15 (parameter p)\u003cbr\u003e\n257|                - m \u003d 0.1 (parameter m)\u003cbr\u003e\n258|                - 0 ≤ u ≤ 5π (lengthwise parameter)\u003cbr\u003e\n259|                - 0 ≤ v ≤ 2π (cross-section parameter)\n260|            \u003c/div\u003e\n261|        \u003c/div\u003e\n262|        \n263|        \u003cdiv id\u003d\&quot;canvas-holder\&quot;\u003e\n264|            \u003ccanvas width\u003d\&quot;800\&quot; height\u003d\&quot;600\&quot; id\u003d\&quot;webglcanvas\&quot; style\u003d\&quot;background-color:black\&quot;\u003e\u003c/canvas\u003e\n265|        \u003c/div\u003e\n266|        \n267|        \u003cdiv class\u003d\&quot;controls-panel\&quot;\u003e\n268|            \u003ch3\u003eSurface Parameters\u003c/h3\u003e\n269|            \u003cdiv class\u003d\&quot;parameter-row\&quot;\u003e\n270|                \u003clabel class\u003d\&quot;parameter-labe