 shader sources from the loaded file\n\n### Conclusion\n\n**You are using the correct shader file.** The `shaders.js` file is:\n1. Properly linked in the HTML\n2. Contains the full Phong lighting model implementation\n3. Is actively being used in your rendering code\n\n**Do NOT switch to shader.gpu** as it:\n1. Contains only basic vertex transformation and solid color rendering\n2. Has no lighting calculations at all\n3. Would not satisfy your requirement for Phong lighting\n\nThe current issue with lighting visibility is related to material properties and normal calculations, not which shader file is being used. The improvements I made to `cornucopia3.js` were designed to address these issues while continuing to use your correctly implemented Phong shaders from `shaders.js`.&quot;}]},{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;can you log for me in shaders where it actually called the light&quot;}],&quot;context&quot;:[{&quot;file_path&quot;:&quot;index.html&quot;,&quot;code_text&quot;:&quot;\u003c!DOCTYPE html\u003e\r\n\u003chtml\u003e\r\n\u003chead\u003e\r\n    \u003cmeta http-equiv\u003d\&quot;Content-Type\&quot; content\u003d\&quot;text/html; charset\u003dUTF-8\&quot;\u003e\r\n    \u003ctitle\u003eCornucopia Surface - WebGL Visualization with Phong Shading\u003c/title\u003e\r\n    \u003cstyle\u003e\r\n        body {\r\n            background-color: #111;\r\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\r\n            color: #fff;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            margin: 0;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        h1, h2 {\r\n            color: #0f0;\r\n        }\r\n        h1 {\r\n            margin-top: 10px;\r\n            font-size: 28px;\r\n        }\r\n        h2 {\r\n            font-size: 22px;\r\n            margin-top: 25px;\r\n        }\r\n        .container {\r\n            max-width: 1000px;\r\n            margin: 0 auto;\r\n            padding: 20px;\r