pt src\u003d\&quot;./test-shader.js\&quot;\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\n```\n\n### What to Look For:\n\n1. **Alert Messages**: \n   - You should see alert messages when the page loads\n   - This confirms the shader files are being loaded\n\n2. **Red Model**:\n   - The model should appear bright red\n   - This confirms the shaders are being compiled and used correctly\n\n3. **Console Output**:\n   - Open your browser\u0027s developer console (F12) to see any error messages\n   - Look for any WebGL errors that might be occurring\n\n### If You Don\u0027t See Red:\n\nIf the model doesn\u0027t turn red, there may be fundamental issues with how WebGL is working in your project:\n1. WebGL context might not be properly initialized\n2. Shaders might not be compiled or linked correctly\n3. There might be errors in the rendering pipeline\n\nTry refreshing the page with these changes, and you should either see a red model (confirming shader loading works) or get clear error messages that will help us identify the issue.&quot;}]},{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;TEST-SHADER.JS LOADED: SHOULD MAKE MODEL RED\ncornucopia3.js:2 Uncaught ReferenceError: updateLightPosition is not defined\n    at cornucopia3.js:2:27&quot;}],&quot;context&quot;:[{&quot;file_path&quot;:&quot;cornucopia3.js&quot;,&quot;code_text&quot;:&quot;    // Update light position for animation\r\n    const lightPosition \u003d updateLightPosition();\r\n    \r\n    // Apply transformations (right to left)\r\n    modelViewMatrix \u003d m4.multiply(moveBack, modelViewMatrix);\r\n    \r\n    // Calculate the combined model-view-projection matrix\r\n    const mvpMatrix \u003d m4.multiply(projectionMatrix, modelViewMatrix);\r\n    \r\n    // Calculate normal matrix (for transforming normals)\r\n    const normalMatrix \u003d calculateNormalMatrix(modelViewMatrix, new Float32Array(9));\r\n    \r\n    // Set shader uniforms\r\n    gl.uniformMatrix